{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Baked Risotto of Smoked Haddock & Leek",
  "text": "Baked Risotto of Smoked Haddock & Leek\n\nPreparation time: 5 mins\n\nCooking time: 35 mins\n\nYield: 4\n\nIngredients\n\nsmall knob of butter,\n\n1 large leek (thinly sliced),\n\n300 g risotto rice,\n\n700 ml fish or vegetable stock,\n\n250 ml full-fat milk,\n\n375 g smoked haddock (skinned and cut into large chunks),\n\n3 tbsp crème fraîche,\n\n100g baby spinach.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Heat oven to 200C/180C fan/gas 6.\n\n2. Heat the butter in a large ovenproof dish over a medium heat.\n\n3. Cook the leek for 4-5 mins, stirring regularly, until just tender.\n\n4. Add the rice and stir for a further 2 mins.\n\n5. Add the stock and milk, bring to the boil and bubble for 5 mins.\n\n6. Put the haddock on top.\n\n7. Cover and bake in the oven for 18 mins until the rice is tender.\n\n8. Fold in the crème fraîche and spinach, season with plenty of black pepper, then cover the pan again and leave to rest out of the oven for 3 mins to allow the spinach to soften.",
  "prepTime": "PT5M",
  "cookTime": "PT35M",
  "recipeYield": "4",
